overall_assessment:
Where it stands: the island is roughly one targeted wave away from a cohesive first iteration, and no map needs a structural rework. All 25 maps build, pass traversal, are reciprocally linked and are under budget. Map-level quality is high: 4 maps are excellent, 20 good and 1 needs work (40002), up from 1/9/15 in iter1. Southperry, the Mushroom Town maps, Amherst, Arch Rock, the Dangerous Forest and Tomato Field all read as classic MapleStory.

Significant issues still remain, because the island layer and the deliverables lag the maps:
- the representative Gameplay renders are missing their player or characters (60000 and 10000 confirmed; 1000005 and 1000006 have no player at all);
- the cloud regression shows in every island shot;
- 25 of 40 trail ends z-fight with map ground, on the main route;
- two deliverables (renders/final and an up-to-date manifest) are not produced.

What matters most next, in sequence:

Wave 0 (lead; land before map authors start, because map builds import mapkit, kit and geo; don't change shared code while fixers run):
- shared #3 player_in_gameplay_frame (plus mobs in frame);
- #10 route-graph check;
- #6 rope asset;
- #5 main-road constant;
- #12 OVERVIEW_EXTRA;
- #14 stairs landing skip;
- #11 grass_rock;
- #15 validator accuracy.

Map wave (parallel, in priority order): 60000 (sails, framing, lighthouse, the ToLedgeRopes step), 40002 (open the crest, paint the through-route), 40000 (two real route steps, valley trees, the floating islet), 20000, 1000000, 30000, 1000001, 1000006, 1000005, 1000002. Every main-route map also switches its through-route ribbon to M_Main_Road; that is a one-liner, because m.path already takes mat=. I omitted 1010001 and 1010002: neither has a material issue, and neither has a prop within 0.45 m of a route. Interiors got a list only for props under 0.45 m from a route.

World/trails work alongside the map wave (it touches only world.py, trails.py and layout.py): #1 clouds, #2 trail junctions with the trail-walk check, #4 runway trails and layout retune, #8 Mushroom Town framing, #9 waterfall, #13 hidden lane and bridge ending, then #16 if time allows.

Then: integrated rebuild → validate (aim for all 'yes', including props_near_routes, orphan_routes and the trail walk) → #7 docs, manifest and renders/final → a short final look at the island, region and Gameplay renders.

Several shared items have slipped once already and are marked as second requests: iter1 #4 junctions, #6 landing skip, #12 main road, #13 grass_rock, 3e long trails, 9d halos.

Conflicts I resolved:
- Lighthouse: uniform scale of about 19-20 m, per iter1's triage. The 32-35 m request is rejected.
- Ropes: keep r 0.07, but hang the strand plumb against the face with no crook on top.
- Mushroom Town: world framing plus landmark scale-ups, and no invented houses, since one house per map is on-data.
- Main road: my own read of Island_WorldMapStyle (stubs only) breaks the tie in favour of making it continuous.

Dropped as wrong or not worth it: reversing the 'no more houses' rule; raising the lighthouse to 32-35 m; the 60001 Eave_Lashed clipping claim (a BODY_Z false positive); per-map work on the 1000004 trellises (a validator false positive).

After this wave, I expect the island to be walkable and verifiably connected, with a traceable cream main road, clean portal junctions, soft clouds, characters in every Gameplay frame and complete deliverables. That is a cohesive first iteration.

Iteration Two candidates:
- a shared Mushroom Town plinth, so 0, 10000 and 20000 sit on one knoll with at-grade village lanes;
- underside crags and hanging spires, SEA_Z at about -420, underside material lightening and one continuous cliff material;
- rim bays and promontories, a coastal palm and sand treatment east of Southperry, and plinth outline wobble if it was not done in #4;
- a kit grass_moss/grass_dark terrain style, skirt-style inheritance and a gloom filler palette for the Dangerous Forest, removing its private-API material swaps;
- code debt: the 1000002 _vine copy, the climb_route and _check_climb workarounds, a crate_block collider, a stored climb_xy instead of loose vertices, a 'passable' tag registry instead of name words, a 3-ray blocking test, z_from stored on routes, and checking non-instance _Architecture meshes;
- landings or dog-legs on the 30 m main-road stair trails, and tapering the 40000→40001 ramp flank;
- grass hop-ramp shading and side skirts, ribbon lip flaps on the 1000000 road, a softer threshold decal, the 1010002 BackGarden ribbon flap;
- a single marker for paired portals 7 m apart (Amherst in01 / Townstreet out00);
- layout-level identity items: the 1000000 sunken hollow with a twin-door mound, 1000002 arriving from the top, the 1000004 free-standing door mound;
- smaller map polish: a 20000 lawn ramp, breaking up 30000's cliff faces, an Amherst market band and Mystic Door markers, a 1010003 front-floor display, the 20001 apex hairline, Southperry barrel engines and ship scale if they were skipped;
- ground-detail scatter on hill skirts and groves on the south-garden skirts;
- a visual link between each interior and its exterior door.
